        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2^{x+1}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\times2^x&=2^1\\times2^x\\\\&=2^{x+1}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence explain why $2^x+2^x$ can be written as $2^{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "There are two equal terms, so $2^x+2^x=2\\times2^x=2^{x+1}$.",
          "worked": "The sum contains two copies of $2^x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2^x+2^x&=2\\times2^x\\\\&=2^{x+1}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What is the highest common factor of these two terms: $2^{x+1}$ and $2^x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2^x$",
          "worked": "$2^{x+1}=2\\times2^x$, so the highest common factor is $2^x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Therefore, factorise $2^{x+1}+2^x$ by taking out the highest common factor.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2^x(2+1)=3\\times2^x$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^{x+1}+2^x&=2\\times2^x+2^x\\\\&=2^x(2+1)\\\\&=3\\times2^x\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-factorising-grid",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
